oth metaphorically  and  literally the voice work and dialogue  while hitting some normal anime tropes  feels a little bit more realistic and  believable compared to previous titles  and the semi-washed out environments and  the more adult looking characters  brings a very welcome new palette change  traversing the world can be engaging as  well with a system of limited cp  or cure points which are tied to healing  support abilities  and taking down blocked terrain in the  world this creates a system where you  simply can't spam healing as a primary  way to refill cure points is by resting  at an inn or at a campground  thinking critically about when and where  to use your precious resource points as  you're playing brings an interesting  layer to the simple dungeon aspect  and gives it more of a feeling of being  a dungeon run rather than simply walking  around and fighting baddies  although this could be a system that can  be seen as an annoyance to some players  oh and as a first in the tail series you  can jump while exploring and access new  areas  nothing mind-boggling but as a longtime  tails fan this is definitely a welcome  new addition  combat is back in its frenetic and  conventional tales formula with  combos arts apple gels and all you'll be  hitting standard attacks with the goal  of breaking the enemy's guard and  continuing your combo  including launching them to get some  extra aerial hits in  defensive abilities such as blocking  dodge rolls and perfect dodge  rolls into counter attacks are all  present as well boost attacks fill in a  gauge over time that can be used to call  in allies at key moments to cover gaps  in combos  or assist attacks while you heal up and  each character has unique abilities that  only they can perform such as special hp  sacrificing powerful attacks that iron  mask can do  and a special bomb attack that xion can  snipe to do more damage  this being a chapter 1 preview build we  obviously couldn't see the whole extent  o